{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/471258-jumping-a-lot","id":471258,"title":"Jumping a lot...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-07T08:50:26-07:00","id":471258,"title":"Jumping a lot...","content":"I know that the topic might be... strange, but here's the question that I received. My players want to know, how high can you jump with Strength 5, Vigor 5 and Celerity 5. They did some &quot;math&quot; and came up somehow with vampires being able to jump 10.000 meters high... Told them that that's impossible, but now we need to know for real, how high can the vampire jump with those stats...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1191-rosencroft","name":"Rosencroft","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T09:03:57-07:00","id":471319,"title":"","content":"Well, I don't think Celerity has anything to do with it.<br /> <br /> Under Vigor it says, 'Additionally, the vampire may make a Strength + Athletics roll to jump. The yards (meters) jumped are equal to (successes) * (Vigor dots + 1).' Normal jumping is Strength + Athletics where the successes equal a vertical foot per success, so this seems to be Vigor specific.<br /> <br /> If you have 5 Strength and 5 Vigor, that gives you an effective Strength of 10. You didn't give us Athletics, but lets say it's between 0 and 5. You have a dicepool between 10 and 15. Then you just multiply the successes by 6. So at the most, with Athletics 5 and all successes in a dicepool of 15, you would jump 90 meters. All successes in a dicepool of 10, with 0 Athletics, you get 60 meters.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind you could have a specialization for jumping or willpower to push yourself higher. Also 10s would allow you to roll again conceivably getting more.<br /> <br /> For a sense of scale, you can see here that 90 meters is just under the height of the Statue of Liberty, and well above a space shuttle.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://eurusenergy.com/wp-content/uploads/2009/02/size_chart.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-07-2015, 12:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T09:10:47-07:00","id":471325,"title":"","content":"Vigor says <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">&quot;Additionally, the vampire may make a Strength + Athletics roll to jump. The yards (meters) jumped are equal to (successes) * (Vigor dots + 1). </span>&quot;<br /> <br /> So that means we got 15 dice for the roll (assuming Athletics 5), which will average us 5 successes, which get's multiplied by 6, so we got ourselves an average of 30 meters jumps.<br /> <br /> If we want want to do some crazy magic with 9-8-agains and perhaps Rote, we could go higher than that... but it will barely exceed a 100 meters.<br /> <br /> Of course, if we also take more dice through Blood (1 vitae -&gt; 2 dice) we could further stretch that... but there's no way that can go up to 10.000.<br /> <br /> Also Celerity does not help in jumping whatsoever <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Imagine Celerity as a speed booster and not a force booster. You can jump up really fast, but you won't jump higher than you would have normally <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's also interesting how Vigor 1 quadruples your jump distances compared to jumping without it. Since normal jumping is Successes/3 meters, and that is overriden by Vigor to provide more jumping power <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T09:11:09-07:00","id":471326,"title":"","content":"Thank you nofather and Griautis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1191-rosencroft","user":"Rosencroft","date":". 04-07-2015, 12:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1191-rosencroft","name":"Rosencroft","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T13:41:36-07:00","id":471617,"title":"","content":"Well, your dicepool is going to go up to 54 dice if you have BP 10, Strength 10, Vigor 5, Athletics 5, three Athletics specialities in Jumping REALLY High, dump 14 Vitae on Physical Intensity, and are spending Willpower on the roll (we <i>really</i> need to make this jump, you guys). If you get all successes on that roll, you have 324 meters.<br /> <br /> High, but not as high as they're saying.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T14:30:15-07:00","id":471691,"title":"","content":"Of course, thanks to 10-again, any arbitrarily high jump height is theoretically achievable, albeit astronomically unlikely, with or without Vigor. But yeah, somewhere around 350 meters is about the most you can realistically expect, and that's if you're dumping EVERYTHING into making your jumping dice pool as high as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T15:22:05-07:00","id":471732,"title":"","content":"A strix with Hollow Bones can triple that, mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T15:22:26-07:00","id":471733,"title":"","content":"...And then the Vampire turns into a fine red shower of blood and guts, upon contact with the earth. That is, if the friction with the air doesn't burn him up first.<br /> <br /> Its kinda late, but after some quick number crunching, it seems like he would accelerate at about 9*G's to reach that hight and upon his eventual contact with the ground, would impact at around 300 km/h, assuming the Vampires weights an average of about 80 kg. I wasn't kidding about the spontaneous combustation part either. I am making alot of rather fishy assumptions here, but I calculated the energy deposited in him due to drag with the air, to be slightly higher than a pretty hefty granade.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T15:29:38-07:00","id":471740,"title":"","content":"You're forgetting terminal velocity. Take-off would be way worse than landing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T15:32:40-07:00","id":471745,"title":"","content":"I believe Satchel pointed out that damage from falling caps at 10 Lethal, something a vampire could likely survive.<br /> <br /> Though at a certain point vampires going splat meets the rule of cool better than vampires being able to leap tall buildings in a single bound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T15:34:42-07:00","id":471747,"title":"","content":"Actually, do vamps downgrade falling damage to bashing or not? I think the same logic as used for everything else holds well enough...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T18:34:32-07:00","id":471928,"title":"","content":"Since intense trauma causes Lethal even to vampires (see rules for hitting vamps with Vigor-lifted objects) I think a fall of that extremity would deal Lethal too. As has been said, though, a vampire can survive it thanks to Resilience and even without that they likely end up in torpor first (but probably need a buddy to save them from the sun then).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T18:42:47-07:00","id":471952,"title":"","content":"Eh, I would rule of cool it. If they can jump like that under their own power, they should be able to land also.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T18:45:11-07:00","id":471953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/471258-jumping-a-lot?p=471747#post471747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, do vamps downgrade falling damage to bashing or not? I think the same logic as used for everything else holds well enough...</div> </div> </div> </div>They do, but a fall like that, I would rule as Agg under the chunky salsa rule, so a vampire would downgrade it to Lethal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T22:29:33-07:00","id":472220,"title":"","content":"I don't think Chunky Salsa is actually a thing outside of Shadowrun.<br /> <br /> Strength 5, Athletics 5, Relevant Specialty with the merit to make it +2, Protean 2, Vigor 5, Professional Training (Athlete) 5, Blood Potency 5, Frenzy<br /> <br /> Looking at (5+5+2+5+10+5) = 32 dice with Rote and 9-again for an average of 22.66667... Successes or 22 * 6 (Vigor) * 2 (Protean 2) = 264 meters. Also the Vampire can glide back down and survive the fall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T01:12:54-07:00","id":472356,"title":"","content":"I've never played Shadowrun and had no idea chunky salsa was a thing in it. I was just using the phrase as a shorthand for &quot;extreme trauma that destroys a significant portion of the body&quot; which in WoD does cause aggravated damage to humans and lethal damage to vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}